Columbia, which comprise ILINet, has ranged from 1.2% to 4.6% and was at or above the national baseline of 2.0% from the week ending November 30, 2013 (week 48) to February 8, 2014 (week 6).","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":826,"renderedHeight":495,"naturalWidth":826,"naturalHeight":495,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 709 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":22188},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/figures/m6307a3f3.gif","alt":"The figure above shows rates of hospitalization for laboratory-confirmed influenza, by age group and surveillance week during 2013–14. CDC monitors hospitalizations associated with laboratory-confirmed influenza in adults and children through the Influenza Hospitalization Surveillance Network (FluSurv-Net), which covers approximately 27 million persons, 8.5% of the U.S. population. From October 1, 2013 through February 8, 2014 (week 6), a total of 6,655 laboratory-confirmed influenza-associated hospitalizations were reported. This yields a rate of 24.6 hospitalizations per 100,000 population.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":646,"renderedHeight":579,"naturalWidth":646,"naturalHeight":579,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 599 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":17752},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/figures/m6307a3f4.gif","alt":"The figure above shows the percentage of laboratory-confirmed influenza hospitalizations and influenza-associated deaths, by age group and influenza seasons, according to FluSurv-NET and 122 U.S. Cities Mortality Reporting System during the 2010–14 influenza seasons. Persons aged ≥65 years had the highest influenza-associated hospitalization rate (50.9 per 100,000), followed by those aged 50–64 years (38.7 per 100,000), 0–4 years (35.9 per 100,000), 18–49 years (16.8 per 100,000), and 5–17 years (6.6 per 100,000). Of the 6,655 influenza-associated hospitalizations that have been reported, 9.4% were reported in persons aged 0–4 years, 4.5% in those aged 5–17 years, 61.2% in those aged 18–64 years, and 24.8% in those aged ≥65 years.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":819,"renderedHeight":364,"naturalWidth":819,"naturalHeight":364,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 740 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":19287},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/images/icon_pdf.gif","alt":"Adobe PDF file","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":16,"renderedHeight":16,"naturalWidth":16,"naturalHeight":16,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":6058},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/images/icon_word.gif","alt":"Microsoft Word file","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":16,"renderedHeight":16,"naturalWidth":16,"naturalHeight":16,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":1087},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/images/icon_excel.gif","alt":"Microsoft Excel file","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":16,"renderedHeight":16,"naturalWidth":16,"naturalHeight":16,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":644},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/images/icon_ppt.gif","alt":"Microsoft PowerPoint file","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":1